    "['delete set protocols bgp group [group_name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper delete commands to equivalent HUAWEI commands:\\n\\n##\\nundo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable\\nundo ipv6-family unicast\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The \"delete set protocols bgp group external neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate\" translates to \"undo peer ... enable\" in HUAWEI, which disables the BGP peer.\\n2. The other delete commands related to IPv6 family settings are consolidated into \"undo ipv6-family unicast\" which removes the IPv6 address family configuration for the BGP peer in HUAWEI.\\n3. The local-address deletion isn\\'t directly translated as HUAWEI handles source address selection differently in BGP configuration.\\n\\nNote that HUAWEI\\'s command structure is more hierarchical and some Juniper concepts don\\'t have direct 1:1 equivalents.', 'trans_template': 'undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo ipv6-family unicast', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'undo ipv6-family unicast', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translation of the Juniper delete commands to equivalent HUAWEI commands:\\n\\n##\\nundo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable\\nundo ipv6-family unicast\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The \"delete set protocols bgp group external neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate\" translates to \"undo peer ... enable\" in HUAWEI, which disables the BGP peer.\\n2. The other delete commands related to IPv6 family settings are consolidated into \"undo ipv6-family unicast\" which removes the IPv6 address family configuration for the BGP peer in HUAWEI.\\n3. The local-address deletion isn\\'t directly translated as HUAWEI handles source address selection differently in BGP configuration.\\n\\nNote that HUAWEI\\'s command structure is more hierarchical and some Juniper concepts don\\'t have direct 1:1 equivalents.', 'trans_template': 'undo ipv6-family unicast'}]]": 1,
    "['neighbor [neighbor_address] activate', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable', 'parent_command': ['undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable'], 'root': 'undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated HUAWEI command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nundo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command `delete set protocols bgp group external neighbor 2001:db8:2::2 activate` is removing the activation of a BGP neighbor\\n- In HUAWEI's VRP, the equivalent command uses `undo peer <ipv6-address> enable` to deactivate a BGP neighbor\\n- The IPv6 address remains the same in the translation\", 'trans_template': 'undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable'}]]": 1,
    "['family [family_type] [address_family] no synchronization', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo ipv6-family unicast synchronization', 'parent_command': ['undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable'], 'root': 'undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nundo ipv6-family unicast synchronization\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Juniper command removes the \"no synchronization\" setting for IPv6 unicast family in BGP, which means enabling synchronization for IPv6 routes.\\n2. In Huawei devices, the equivalent is to undo (remove) the \"synchronization\" setting in the IPv6 address family view.\\n3. The command is placed in the BGP configuration context where the IPv6 address family is configured.', 'trans_template': 'undo ipv6-family unicast synchronization'}]]": 1,
    "['family [parameter2] [parameter3] redistribute [parameter4]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo ipv6-family unicast redistribute connected', 'parent_command': ['undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable'], 'root': 'undo peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated HUAWEI command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nundo ipv6-family unicast redistribute connected\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command removes the redistribution of connected routes in the IPv6 unicast address family under BGP configuration\\n- In HUAWEI's VRP, this is equivalent to using the `undo` command to remove the redistribution of connected routes in the IPv6 unicast address family\\n- The command is placed under the BGP neighbor configuration context in HUAWEI devices\", 'trans_template': 'undo ipv6-family unicast redistribute connected'}]]": 1,
    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ipv6-family unicast', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'bgp [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command to Huawei equivalent for the BGP neighbor configuration:\\n\\n##\\nipv6-family unicast\\npeer 2001:db8:2::2 enable\\n##\\n\\nNote: This is the Huawei equivalent for the Juniper command `set protocols bgp group external neighbor 2001:db8:2::2` combined with `set protocols bgp group external family inet6 unicast`, which activates IPv6 unicast for the specified neighbor. In Huawei, you first enter the IPv6 address family context, then enable the peer for that address family.\", 'trans_template': 'ipv6-family unicast'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command to Huawei equivalent for the BGP neighbor configuration:\\n\\n##\\nipv6-family unicast\\npeer 2001:db8:2::2 enable\\n##\\n\\nNote: This is the Huawei equivalent for the Juniper command `set protocols bgp group external neighbor 2001:db8:2::2` combined with `set protocols bgp group external family inet6 unicast`, which activates IPv6 unicast for the specified neighbor. In Huawei, you first enter the IPv6 address family context, then enable the peer for that address family.\", 'trans_template': 'peer 2001:db8:2::2 enable'}]]": 1,
